General information for Version u238ib58lrlFsfaST4q :             9237 1451
- The basis for cross sections in the fast energy range is        9237 1451
  the Empire ib58 calculation.                                    9237 1451
- The IRMM Resonance file is 238U_H20-43_adopNG3+INL46+TOT+NF_12  9237 1451
  with new resolved/unresolved resonance evaluation.              9237 1451
- Capture cross sections are from Standards-2017 up to 2.2 MeV    9237 1451
- Fission cross corresponds to Standards-2017.                    9237 1451
  In the resolved resonance range some background is added so     9237 1451
  that the fission cross section after resolution broadening      9237 1451
  approximately matches the low-resolution Slovacek data.         9237 1451
- PFNS is as provided by P. Talou for the IAEA CRP on PFNS        9237 1451
  of Actinides. The duplicate entry at 5 MeV is removed (the      9237 1451
  second set is retained). PFNS at 8 MeV and above are taken      9237 1451
  from the JENDL-4.0 evaluation because ENDF/B-VII.1 data have    9237 1451
  have unphysical behaviour, manifested in a decline of E_aver.   9237 1451
- Angular distributions are entirely from the Empire calculation. 9237 1451
- Prompt fission gamma multiplicities were evaluated by           9237 1451
  I. Stetcu (LANL, November 16, 2017). Based on Ref. [Leb2015],   9237 1451
  it was assumed that the U-235 and U-238 multiplicities are      9237 1451
  proportional to each other. Hence, the shape of the             9237 1451
  energy dependence of the average multiplicity for U-238 was     9237 1451
  taken from U5, and rescaled so that the total gamma production  9237 1451
  at 14.3 MeV reproduces Drake [Dr1978]                           9237 1451
  [Leb2017] M.Lebois et. al., Phys. Rev. C 92, 034618 (2015)      9237 1451
  [Dr1978] D.M.Drake, E.D.Arthur, M.G.Silbert,                    9237 1451
  Nuclear Science and Engineering, Vol.65, p.49 (1978)            9237 1451
- The PFGS is based on the JEFF-3.3 (ver T3) evaluation up to     9237 1451
  1 MeV outgoing gamma energies. From 1 MeV up, the spectrum is   9237 1451
  continuous with the u235 spectrum. The same spectrum was used   9237 1451
  for the whole incident neutron energy range.                    9237 1451
- Fission neutron and gamma photon probabilities in the new       9237 1451
  MF 6 format are included.                                       9237 1451
- Covariances in the resonance region are taken from JEFF-3.3,    9237 1451
  including elastic, fission, capture and the corresponding       9237 1451
  cross-reaction covariances. To correct for the "hole" in        9237 1451
  the uncertainty of the elastic cross section, a 4 percent       9237 1451
  uncertainty is added in the range 100 eV - 3 keV.               9237 1451
  The total is defined as the sum of the partials.                9237 1451
- The covariance matrix prior for the cross sections and          9237 1451
  Legendre coefficients of the angular distributions above        9237 1451
  the resolved resonance range is generated using the Monte       9237 1451
  Carlo technique by statistical sampling of the model            9237 1451
  parameter in the Empire calculations. About 3000 ENDF           9237 1451
  files were generated in the process. The first discrete         9237 1451
  inelastic cross section is treated explicitly while all         9237 1451
  the others are lumped into MT 851. Similarly, absorption        9237 1451
  reactions MT649 and MT800 are lumped into MT 852. This          9237 1451
  is necessary to preserve unitarity without defining the         9237 1451
  covariances for each reaction channel separately.               9237 1451
- The final covariance matrices for all reactions (including      9237 1451
  cross reaction correlations) were obtained by the generalised   9237 1451
  least-squares method in the GANDR system using measured         9237 1451
  data from the EXFOR data base, except for fission and           9237 1451
  capture, in which case the Standards-2017 were input            9237 1451
  to GANDR instead of the experimental data.                      9237 1451
  Experimental data marked with * were renormalized to the        9237 1451
  IRDFF-1.05 cross sections @ https://www-nds.iaea.org/IRDFF/.    9237 1451
                                                                  9237 1451
