- Cross-material covariances were prepared manually from the      9237 1451
  Standards-2017 file. Unrecognised sources of uncertainties      9237 1451
  (USU) of 1.2 percent were added to the cross-covariances of     9237 1451
  the fission cross sections, and of 1.7 percent to the           9237 1451
  capture cross sections between different materials.             9237 1451
- The uncertainties of the delayed neutron multiplicities were    9237 1451
  taken from:                                                     9237 1451
  R. J. Tuttle (1975) Delayed-Neutron Data for Reactor-Physics    9237 1451
  Analysis, Nuclear Science and Engineering, 56:1, 37-71,         9237 1451
  DOI: 10.13182/NSE75-A26620                                      9237 1451
- The initial covariances for the prompt fission neutron          9237 1451
  multiplicities were taken from ENDF/B-VII.1, which originated   9237 1451
  from P. Young least-square fit of available nubar data.         9237 1451
  The following modifications were made:                          9237 1451
  * Below 500 keV no measurements are available. The uncertainty  9237 1451
    was arbitrarily set to 2.5 percent.                           9237 1451
  * An additional 0.4 percent was added over the energy           9237 1451
    intervals 0.5 MeV, 4 MeV, 10 MeV, 20 MeV, 30 MeV to account   9237 1451
    for unrecognized systematic uncertaity of nubar measurements  9237 1451
    as recommended in Standards-2017.                             9237 1451
- The covariances of the P1 elastic scattering component          9237 1451
  as obtained in the prior are available in MF34.                 9237 1451
- The PFNS covariances were evaluated with the spectra, but       9237 1451
  they are given only for the energy range up to 5 MeV in MF35.   9237 1451
