 Nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-3.2.3 Malta                   9237 1451
 (SVN rev.  4929; source rev.  4929)                              9237 1451
 by M.W.Herman et al [EMP,EMP-man].                               9237 1451
                                                                  9237 1451
 EMPIRE dimensions (dimension.h):                                 9237 1451
  NDNUC=  50  NDEXCLUS= 10  NDEX= 601  NDLW=  50                  9237 1451
  LEVCC= 30  NDLV= 40  NDBR= 40  NDMSCS= 4                        9237 1451
                                                                  9237 1451
 CROSS-SECTION EVALUATION PROCEDURE                               9237 1451
                                                                  9237 1451
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                9237 1451
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               9237 1451
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             9237 1451
                                                                  9237 1451
 This code integrates into a single system a number               9237 1451
 of important modules and features:                               9237 1451
                                                                  9237 1451
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 9237 1451
   coupled-channels code ECIS06 by J. Raynal                      9237 1451
 - Soft-rotator deformed Optical Model including                  9237 1451
   coupled-channels code OPTMAN by E.Soukhovitskii                9237 1451
   and coworkers                                                  9237 1451
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    9237 1451
   width fluctuation correction, and the                          9237 1451
   optical model for fission with partial damping                 9237 1451
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                9237 1451
   TRISTAN by H.Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                       9237 1451
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      9237 1451
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 9237 1451
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                9237 1451
 - Hybrid Monte Carlo preequilibrium model(M.Blann)               9237 1451
   (code DDHMS by M.Chadwick, mod. by B.V.Carlson)                9237 1451
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   9237 1451
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                9237 1451
   discrete transitions                                           9237 1451
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                9237 1451
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                9237 1451
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               9237 1451
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 9237 1451
   library [RIPL]                                                 9237 1451
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              9237 1451
   EXFOR library                                                  9237 1451
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A.Trkov)                     9237 1451
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 9237 1451
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                9237 1451
   PrePro codes by D. Cullen                                      9237 1451
 - ENDF checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                   9237 1451
 - Highly automated fitting of optical model                      9237 1451
   parameters (by B.V. Carlson)                                   9237 1451
 - KALMAN code for fitting experimental data and                  9237 1451
 - generating covariances                                         9237 1451
 - Support for NJOY                                               9237 1451
                                                                  9237 1451
                                                                  9237 1451
