 *** ENDRESS - Merging source and resonance ENDF files            9237 1451
  Source ENDF u238.e0                                             9237 1451
  Resonance ENDF IRMM\238U_H20-43_adopNG3+INL46+TOT+NF_12.end     9237 1451
                                                                  9237 1451
** OCTOBER 2016                                                 **9237 1451
** Update of RRR & URR in JEFF33T2 (=JEFF33T0)                  **9237 1451
**                                                              **9237 1451
** Update performed by I.Sirakov (INRNE,Sofia) in collaboration **9237 1451
**        with the EC-JRC Geel, the IAEA (Vienna), and          **9237 1451
**  with support by the OECD Nuclear Energy Agency - NEA (Paris)**9237 1451
**                                                              **9237 1451
** VERSION H20-43 with LSSF=1 and:                              **9237 1451
** - JRC Geel update #2 of the resolved resonance parameters    **9237 1451
**   below 1.2 keV through simultaneous analysis [8] (2016) of  **9237 1451
**   GELINA capture and ORNL transmission data.                 **9237 1451
** - Adoption of four unresolved infinitely dilute cross        **9237 1451
**   sections - capture, inelastic, total and fission.          **9237 1451
**                                                              **9237 1451
**A) Particular URR characteristics of this version:            **9237 1451
** - Lower URR limit at 20 keV.                                 **9237 1451
** - Adoption of the infinitely dilute capture cross section    **9237 1451
**   from the Pronyaev's GMA evaluation on the available (n,g)  **9237 1451
**   data for U-238 [7] (2016).                                 **9237 1451
** - Adoption of the infinitely dilute inelastic cross section  **9237 1451
**   from the neutron scattering evaluation 'ib46' of Capote et **9237 1451
**   al.[4-5] (2016), with a direct inelastic part given by the **9237 1451
**   DCCOM with RIPL 2412 OMP [3-4].                            **9237 1451
** - Adoption of the infinitely dilute total cross section from **9237 1451
**   the Pronyaev's GMA evaluation on the available transmission**9237 1451
**   data for U-238 [6] (2014) (see URR description).           **9237 1451
** - Adoption of the infinitely dilute fission cross section    **9237 1451
**   from the Trkov's estimation on the available sub-threshold **9237 1451
**   fission data for U-238 [9] (2016).                         **9237 1451
**                                                              **9237 1451
**B) Common URR characteristics for all H versions:             **9237 1451
** - Neutron strength functions determined so as to reproduce   **9237 1451
**   the compound absorption cross sections of the DCCOM with   **9237 1451
**   RIPL 2412 OMP [3-4].                                       **9237 1451
** - Hard-sphere scattering radius optimized on the GMA non-    **9237 1451
**   model total cross section evaluation derived by V.Pronyaev **9237 1451
**   [6].                                                       **9237 1451
** - Capture transmission coefficients determined in a fit to   **9237 1451
**   the Pronyaev's GMA non-model capture cross section         **9237 1451
**   evaluation [7].                                            **9237 1451
** - Effective <Gg(l=0)> obtained by extracting the average Gg  **9237 1451
**   from analysis of GELINA data below 1.2 keV [8], and        **9237 1451
**   projecting its value to a mid energy point of 75 keV       **9237 1451
**   through the GDR-model (see URR description). That          **9237 1451
**   represents the main difference with the L-versions, which  **9237 1451
**   <Gg(l=0)> has directly been extracted from the data        **9237 1451
**   analysis below 1.2 keV. The magnitude of such adjustments  **9237 1451
**   in the alternative H- and L-versions ranges up to 0.8 meV  **9237 1451
**   in <Gg(l=0)> and 0.8 eV in D0 retaining the fitted capture **9237 1451
**   transmission coefficients practically intact.              **9237 1451
**                                                              **9237 1451
